  "economy": {
    "canonical_prices": [],
    "price_claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is also called a movable primeval spring, with a daily output priced at fifty primeval stones. By the Shang clan city stretch he still keeps it, notes he lacks the recipe to advance it further, and expects its help to become negligible once he reaches rank four.",
        "chapters": [
          273
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-yuan-obtains-the-lotus",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_shang_clan_city"
        ],
        "needs_review": true
      }
    ],
    "game_proposals": []
  },
  "distribution": {
    "locations": [],
    "factions": [
      "fac_gu_yue_clan"
    ],
    "origin": "unknown",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan reads the scene as the end of the Flower Wine Monk inheritance. Centuries earlier the Monk, already knowing the refinement recipe and lacking only a natural spirit spring, secretly refined the lotus in the Gu Yue clan spring after fighting the fourth generation clan leader.",
        "chapters": [
          163
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "gu-yue-foundation-stakes",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "inh_flower_wine_monk_inheritance",
          "fac_gu_yue_clan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Immortal Venerable Genesis Lotus, a righteous faction Gu Master, created the lotus’s fusion recipe many millennia ago. The rank three lotus has an advancement route up to rank six Heavenly Essence Treasure Imperial Lotus, named sixth among the Top Ten Great Immortal Gu and priced near Spring Autumn Cicada in worth. Refinement demands a natural spirit spring that is still full of primeval energy, not a long-used spring whose reserves are drying out. Success ends that spring’s ability to produce primeval stones. Advancing further is said to need seven springs at rank four, nine at rank five, and eleven at rank six, plus precious auxiliary Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          163
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "gu-yue-foundation-stakes",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master",
          "gu_white_form_immortal_snake",
          "gu_spring_autumn_cicada",
          "sys_refinement"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The lotus must grow nine intact leaves before it can be plucked into an aperture. Fang Yuan finds eight leaves and a damaged half leaf, because the lotus has been compensating for a spring drained across generations, and he estimates over fifty thousand primeval stones are needed to restore that leaf at once. He also judges that removing the lotus would make the spring completely useless, force a frantic clan investigation, and leave Gu Yue clan without the foundation that has sustained it on that mountain for close to a millennium. In his reading, the Monk left the setup as revenge: whether the pluck succeeds or fails, the spring is finished, and without it the clan cannot remain.",
        "chapters": [
          163
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "gu-yue-foundation-stakes",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
